2026-11-01  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/input.cpp (token::next): Throw warning in
	category "style" if the input uses `\\` to try to format a
	backslash, which is not reliable if the escape character is
	changed (you then get _two_ backslashes instead).  Emit warning
	in category "escape" if encountering an escaped dot.  This
	member function operates only in interpretation mode, so no
	false positives occur when using `\` to escape a dot in copy
	mode, as is sometimes done when nesting macro definitions.

	Fixes <https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?68361>.

2026-11-01  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/input.cpp: Refactor.  Apply DRY principle.
	(maybe_warn_about_portability): New `static` `inline` function
	replaces 18 instances of open-coded logic in...
	(token::next): ...this member function.

2026-11-01  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/input.cpp (token::next): Refactor to simplify.
	Stop wrapping `delete` operation with null pointer check.

2026-11-02  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/div.cpp (need_vertical_space_request): Revise
	`ne` request behavior; perform no operation if the argument is
	invalid.  Our documentation already said this was the case, but
	while the request threw an error diagnostic, it proceeded as if
	`.ne 1v` (or, equivalently, simply `.ne`) had been specified.

	Fixes <https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?68868>.

